#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046645} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534127} :activity/id #uuid "72200359-34e6-5d5b-9196-498c2e2739b8" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050228 :topic/id #uuid "37d183d8-ce59-581c-9a89-fec7544aae03" :topic/math-academy-id 6376} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534109 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533984 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21f04a48-e3d9-5285-9be6-a47bfb7a3162" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{L4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533221} {:answer/id #uuid "806ffe8b-ec3d-5752-b9c6-7e479c231b96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{L2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533443} {:answer/id #uuid "bf7ddf96-482e-5261-9f56-9cabb5f0cd3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{L1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533600} {:answer/id #uuid "d4ac113d-a092-55a0-828c-3cce578364b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{L3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533658}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533443} :answer-field/id #uuid "047d2299-ba3b-5217-bd76-392b196edadf" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533773} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "175e98b0-2179-5c38-aec4-02ea135fddfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{Φ}^{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533192} {:answer/id #uuid "4fb78a1e-acbc-582f-9896-4a25b60643c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "Φ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533330} {:answer/id #uuid "85fcf6d7-1b0b-5bf0-afee-87974db835f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533455} {:answer/id #uuid "ce4797d8-fe35-5b5b-b08e-1c83d6082952" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{A}^{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533639}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533330} :answer-field/id #uuid "20fff794-00dd-50a8-9256-5d3d679c4c80" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533806} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fa5012c-8bff-5182-bdc1-c3192d2fa42b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "properties of diagonalizable matrices" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533179} {:answer/id #uuid "c9a4e473-005c-5bad-b050-c349b4619ab7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "integrating the given system" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533622} {:answer/id #uuid "cfe5eb6f-4d7a-5247-87cc-a29690e1564d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "definition of matrix multiplication" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533644} {:answer/id #uuid "e959566f-e723-58b3-9ab2-a51a923ed3cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "definition of a fundamental matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533714}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533714} :answer-field/id #uuid "99e500e9-2419-5436-86f7-bd0983f12961" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533896} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a59e584-278d-59db-b6ea-7b7977de0f71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "columns" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533159} {:answer/id #uuid "79c8042c-d474-5943-aed4-1c689601cb7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "diagonals" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533428} {:answer/id #uuid "b483bb15-790a-5e86-a64e-5ba317eecac7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "first row" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533578} {:answer/id #uuid "cc4405cf-0772-5f28-9f99-4a05e4a8fb85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "rows" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533632}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533159} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8b3efd3-b7c3-58e8-b4b9-9e7263c863ee" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533964}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "20281150-3bf1-5302-a5be-765695a3b8d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-336094" :question/problem "Consider the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant $2\\times 2$ matrix. Let $Φ(t)$ be a fundamental matrix for this system. A derivation showing that $Φ(t)$ is invertible for all $t$ is given below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ be the columns of $Φ(t)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are linearly independent for all $t$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $det(Φ(t))\\ne 0$ for all $t$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $Φ(t)$ is invertible for all $t$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L1}$ introduces the notation for the {{field-1}} of {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the {{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from line {{field-4}} by the properties of determinants." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first interpret line $\\text{L1}.$ Line $\\text{L1}$ introduces the notation for the $\\text{columns}$ of $Φ,$ namely the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t).$ These functions are the fundamental solutions of the system.\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Since $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ form a basis of the solution space for our system. Thus, $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the $\\text{definition of a fundamental matrix}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Recall that a matrix has linearly independent columns if and only if its determinant is nonzero. Since ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are linearly independent for any particular $t,$\n\n$$\ndet(Φ(t))\\ne 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L3}$ follows from line $\\text{L2}$ by the properties of determinants."} :step/id #uuid "231eb329-513b-5dfb-85da-6e0f13afe8fd"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534111 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398781 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c007ca0-acef-5af6-b3fe-264373817071" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2{e}^{-1} & 2{e}^{-1} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-1}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398783} {:answer/id #uuid "59ce7ec4-615c-508f-9c8e-4b5a5d18d797" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-t} & 0 \\\\ 2t{e}^{-t} & 2{e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398784} {:answer/id #uuid "b333daa7-d3c9-5885-83dd-c52477a27945" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2t \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398785} {:answer/id #uuid "1281b7c7-c44e-5d28-ae85-689e0d3ae235" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2{e}^{-t} & 2t{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398786} {:answer/id #uuid "de8dcb0a-6338-525e-8932-5efde71571f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398787}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398786} :answer-field/id #uuid "f91e0298-1d33-5125-a1ef-22a1c3b27757" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398782}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6ce970ec-3f9d-57d6-9307-1253ccd1b689" :question/math-academy-id "q-334326" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}x,\\,{x}_{1}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t},\\,{x}_{2}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2t \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs and two of its linearly independent solutions ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2},$ shown above. Which of the following is a fundamental matrix for the system?" :question/worked-solution "Given a linear system ${x}^{′}=Ax,$ where $A$ is an $n\\times n$ matrix, a *fundamental matrix* $Φ(t)$ of the system is an $n\\times n$ matrix whose columns are linearly independent solutions of the system.\n\nIn our case, we have a $2\\times 2$ system. We are also given that the two linearly independent solutions of the system are the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}=\\begin{bmatrix}2{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}2t \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}=\\begin{bmatrix}2t{e}^{-t} \\\\ {e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our fundamental could be written as\n\n$$\nΦ(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2{e}^{-t} & 2t{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Note:** The columns of $Φ$ can be written in any order."} :step/id #uuid "24523b4e-4e57-53cd-8b40-7f56c7c2589e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534142}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534127 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221991 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b918900-9d47-501a-8fe9-03921f6ed92d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "properties of invertible matrices" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305722} {:answer/id #uuid "5dbdc32e-065c-5332-9d8e-eb72d3130e00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "definition of a fundamental matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306051} {:answer/id #uuid "6b45a51c-d763-5bfb-9f79-8f1fadd5a426" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "definition of a fundamental matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306178} {:answer/id #uuid "6d2b391a-a7cf-5a3f-b395-8b5343a7d633" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "properties of diagonalizable matrices" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306196} {:answer/id #uuid "d400de09-c2d8-5f6f-8258-d35170cbcf5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "definition of matrix multiplication" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307116}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306051} :answer-field/id #uuid "97f4577b-63be-5c98-bcf0-c658896d4179" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307999} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c29a02a-5ddf-5ffe-8562-988f1e1a9aff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "the definition of a basis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305255} {:answer/id #uuid "316d241a-8a8a-5270-84e3-f0fc3ef40261" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "adding the vectors ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305617} {:answer/id #uuid "39f356a8-8fda-5c4b-9454-f7cb76d1ea0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "integrating the given system" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305702} {:answer/id #uuid "600321e5-9661-57d4-a3e1-64da86996880" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "multiplying $Φ(t)$ with it's inverse" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306076} {:answer/id #uuid "e313c524-01fc-5609-ae4c-14eafceafe00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "the definition of a basis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307255}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305255} :answer-field/id #uuid "9bd31540-fe17-5fac-bdc9-cc5602d470d7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308012} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9df8332a-0028-5851-a541-699e5fb5b445" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "definition of matrix multiplication" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306628} {:answer/id #uuid "a35b581b-96f5-5832-8aa2-3b756a1be5cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "definition of a fundamental matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306689} {:answer/id #uuid "b096b37f-397b-59cd-b45a-7a82f14b6d6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "fact that $Φ$ is nonsingular" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306813} {:answer/id #uuid "edcd7607-2741-5c34-acfc-0d847398cbb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "properties of invertible matrices" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307336} {:answer/id #uuid "edd1095a-2f45-5472-aa18-be05cd67e567" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "definition of matrix multiplication" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307337}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186307337} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5be50c8-6e0b-5b31-b6e5-a6b8db5b8b63" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308245}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7179862e-a345-5508-93d4-73732015d190" :question/math-academy-id "q-333723" :question/problem "Consider the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant $2\\times 2$ matrix. Let $Φ(t)$ be a fundamental matrix for this system. A derivation showing that every solution $x(t)$ can be written in the form $x(t)=Φ(t)\\,c$ for some constant vector $c=[{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}]^{T}$ is given below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ be the columns of $Φ(t)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ form a basis of solutions\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $x(t)$ can be written as $x(t)={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $Φ(t)\\,c={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $x(t)=Φ(t)\\,c$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from line $\\text{L2}$ by {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by the {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Since $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ form a basis of the solution space for our system. Thus, $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the $\\text{definition of a fundamental matrix}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Once ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ form a basis, every solution $x(t)$ of the system can be expressed uniquely as a linear combination\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by $\\text{the definition of a basis}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ Since ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are the columns of $Φ(t),$ we can write\n\n$$\nΦ(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\,| & | \\\\ {x}_{1}(t) & {x}_{2}(t) \\\\ \\,| & |\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThen by the definition of matrix multiplication,\n\n$$\nΦ(t)\\,c=\\begin{bmatrix}\\,| & | \\\\ {x}_{1}(t) & {x}_{2}(t) \\\\ \\,| & |\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t).\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the $\\text{definition of matrix multiplication}.$"} :step/id #uuid "62363ed1-22ab-56fa-9971-8c017f526c79" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534111}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534128 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365673 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5728e179-6831-5401-a928-e641db0a06b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{-4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365675}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365675} :answer-field/id #uuid "afbc2e57-8b1b-5ce4-9b27-cb6cab8bfe1d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365674} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "979acb26-7ddd-5b55-9211-9925729aa071" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365677}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365677} :answer-field/id #uuid "43739f8d-9cc2-5a3f-8f44-3fd681edf8db" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365676} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8029db2d-8bde-50dd-9836-f39ca854a3bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "t{e}^{-4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365679}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365679} :answer-field/id #uuid "faaddf78-a1db-5496-a708-d82d0e79d47b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365678} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6356927b-4df6-547a-97be-5637f834898e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{-4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365681}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365681} :answer-field/id #uuid "c911bdd1-5a68-53a2-90c8-77d2d0783bc8" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365680}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "93c5b9c1-d3c4-52c5-af95-03ae43585aaf" :question/math-academy-id "q-334497" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs ${x}^{′}=Ax$ with the matrix $A$ shown above. Compute the **standard** fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ for this system.\n\n| ${Φ}_{0}(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $A$ is a constant $n\\times n$ matrix and $x(t)$ is an $n\\times 1$ column vector. The standard fundamental matrix of the linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ denoted ${Φ}_{0}(t),$ is the unique matrix solution of the initial value problem \n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere ${I}_{n}$ is the identity matrix. \n\nFurthermore, it can be shown that ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}.$\n\nWe have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{bmatrix}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & {\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ 0 & -4{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are constants to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The only eigenvalue of $At$ is \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=-4t\n$$\n\nof multiplicity two. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}r(-4t) &={e}^{-4t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\lambda }r(-4t) &={e}^{-4t}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-4t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0} &={e}^{-4t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1} &={e}^{-4t}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n- From the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{-4t}.\n$$\n\n- Substituting this into the first one, we get\n\n$$\n-4t{e}^{-4t}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{-4t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{-4t}(1+4t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =-4{e}^{-4t}t+{e}^{-4t}(1+4t) \\\\  & ={e}^{-4t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}t & ={e}^{-4t}t \\\\  & =t{e}^{-4t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-4t} & t{e}^{-4t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-4t}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "6372c740-c40b-54b4-b2d8-d67db30bf1d4" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534109}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534142 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534093 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a54e01d-d3da-520d-a71e-fb2b3d3a8bd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{6t}+e^{-6t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533275}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533275} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ec158fd-889b-5066-b795-fdf52e06926c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533801} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f40c120d-2ef8-574c-b604-70f11f9600d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{6t}+e^{-6t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533740}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533740} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ac691a2-04d5-52ef-bc49-8d3327cd84e3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533851}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "f69ba2b0-76ef-5087-a5bf-906e0adf24a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-334388" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs ${x}^{′}=Ax$ with the matrix $A$ shown above. Compute the **standard** fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ for this system.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">${Φ}_{0}(t)=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">${e}^{6t}-{e}^{-6t}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">${e}^{6t}-{e}^{-6t}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr></tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $A$ is a constant $n\\times n$ matrix and $x(t)$ is an $n\\times 1$ column vector. The standard fundamental matrix of the linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ denoted ${Φ}_{0}(t),$ is the unique matrix solution of the initial value problem \n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere ${I}_{n}$ is the identity matrix. \n\nFurthermore, it can be shown that ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}.$\n\nWe have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}]t+{\\alpha }_{0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} & 6{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ 6{\\alpha }_{1}t & {\\alpha }_{0}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are constants to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues of $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=-6t,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=6t,\n$$\n\neach of multiplicity one. Thus, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}r(-6t)={e}^{-6t} \\\\ r(6t)={e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}-6t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{-6t} \\\\ 6t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n- Subtracting the second equation from the first one, we get\n\n$$\n-12t{\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{-6t}-{e}^{6t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{1}=-\\frac{1}{12t}({e}^{-6t}-{e}^{6t}).\n$$\n\n- Adding the first and the second equations, we get\n\n$$\n2{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{-6t}+{e}^{6t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{0}=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{-6t}+{e}^{6t}).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{-6t}+{e}^{6t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{6t}+{e}^{-6t}) \\\\ 6{\\alpha }_{1}t & =6\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{12t}({e}^{-6t}-{e}^{6t}))t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{6t}-{e}^{-6t})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{6t}+{e}^{-6t} & {e}^{6t}-{e}^{-6t} \\\\ {e}^{6t}-{e}^{-6t} & {e}^{6t}+{e}^{-6t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "a9bd7aaf-ed47-5adf-8e37-bc1f645e1959" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534128}}] :activity/title "Fundamental Matrices" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533125}]}
